  "title": "Five outgoing centers in a 16-realization cube move",
  "description": "This note specifies six fixed algebraic boundary points admitting an incoming alpha=16 realization and at least five distinct outgoing centers. Exact rational bounds, the intermediate value theorem and monotone polynomial root definitions prove the construction. It contradicts the at-most-three expectation in Melotti\u2013Ramassamy\u2013Th\u00e9venin (2023), Remark 4.8, in the realization setting allowing crossings. A fixed boundary crossing excludes proper embeddings. The exact total count and universal maximum remain unknown. The curves are members of the earlier weighted-distance and p-power families of Ash\u2013Bolker (1986), Bourne\u2013Peletier\u2013Roper (2014) and Bourne\u2013Roper (2015). A bounded search through 15 October 2026 located no earlier pure-power four-or-more shared-focus example in its checked corpus; historical priority remains unestablished. AI was used extensively. This preprint is unrefereed and has not received conventional human peer review.",
